      -> for an exponential disk the Freeman formula makes g_b at a
         FIXED multiple of h_R proportional to Sigma_0 with a pure
         constant, so 'local in g_b' and 'global in Sigma_0' are the
         SAME between-galaxy predictor here.  Only the RADIAL shape can
         separate them, and g_b is nearly flat across 0.3-2.0 h_R.

